# nest-erp AI Rules

## Scope
- Monorepo: `backend/` (NestJS), `frontend/` (React/Vite). Separate pnpm apps, not a workspace root.
- API prefix: `api/v1`. All requests require `x-tenant-id` header.
- Do not explain standard library/framework defaults. Output only what changes.

## Output Constraints
- Modified code blocks only; omit unchanged surrounding code (use `// ...` sparingly).
- No tutorial prose, no "here's how X works" for Nest/React/MUI basics.
- No duplicate file headers or re-stating task requirements.
- When editing: name exact file paths; prefer minimal diffs.
- Do not add tests unless requested.
- Do not create commits unless requested.

## Backend (NestJS)

### Structure
- Domain modules: `backend/src/modules/<domain>/` — `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `entities/`, `dto/`, `services/`, `controllers/`.
- Auth: `backend/src/auth/` (not under `modules/`).
- Cross-cutting: `backend/src/common/` (`@Global()` CommonModule).
- Identity: `backend/src/modules/identity/` (`@Global()`).

### Entities
- Extend `BaseEntity` (`id` uuid, `tenantId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `@VersionColumn()`).
- DB columns: snake_case via `name:`; TS properties: camelCase.
- `synchronize: false` — schema changes via migrations only.
- App DB role enforces RLS; admin role for `migration:run`.

### Multi-Tenancy (mandatory)
- Every tenant-scoped write runs inside `TenantTransactionInterceptor` transaction.
- RLS session vars set via `set_config('app.current_tenant_id', ...)` and `app.current_user_id`.
- Inject repos → assign `this.repo = wrapTenantRepository(repoBase)`.
- Manual transactions: `withTenantTransaction(dataSource, ...)` or `createTenantQueryRunner()`.
- Do not rely on manual `WHERE tenant_id =` alone; RLS is the isolation layer.
- JWT `tenantId` must match `x-tenant-id` when both present.

### DTOs & Validation
- `class-validator` + `class-transformer` (`@IsUUID`, `@ValidateNested`, `@Type`).
- `@ApiProperty` / `@ApiPropertyOptional` on all DTO fields.
- DTOs in `dto/` per module; nested subfolders for complex domains (e.g. `auth/dto/passkey/`).
- Global `ValidationPipe({ transform: true })`; route params: `ParseUUIDPipe` (inventory routes: `version: '7'`).
- No custom validation pipes.

### Controllers & Guards
- Stack: `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, PermissionsGuard)` + `@RequirePermissions('action:resource')`.
- Mutating POSTs on Finance/Sales/Procurement/Inventory: add `@Idempotent()` + require `Idempotency-Key` header.
- Permissions format: `action:resource` (e.g. `create:journal`, `read:stock`).

### Services
- Direct cross-module calls via Nest DI imports — no EventEmitter.
- Async external notifications: `WebhookEventHubService.emit()` / `WebhookDispatcherService.dispatch()`.
- Complex writes inside interceptor transaction or `withTenantTransaction()`.

### Naming
- Files: kebab-case + suffix (`journal-entry.service.ts`).
- Classes: PascalCase + suffix (`JournalEntryService`).
- Enums: PascalCase type, UPPER values (`JournalStatus.DRAFT`).

## Frontend (React/Vite)

### Structure
- `src/features/<domain>/` — `{domain}Routes.ts`, `pages/`, `components/`, `schemas/`.
- `src/lib/` — api, auth, i18n, rbac, theme.
- `src/stores/` — global Zustand; feature stores in feature folder (e.g. `pos/posStore.ts`).
- `src/shared/` — layouts, UI primitives, form toolkit.
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`.

### State
- Global Zustand: `useAuthStore`, `usePreferencesStore`, `useNotificationStore`, `useTenantTimezoneStore`.
- Persist via `zustand/middleware` `persist` + `partialize`.
- Imperative access in interceptors: `useAuthStore.getState()`.
- Server state: TanStack Query only — no duplicating API data in Zustand.

### React Query
- Keys: `queryKeys` factory in `src/lib/api/query-keys.ts` — always use, never ad-hoc strings.
- Queries: `src/lib/api/queries/use{Domain}.ts`; mutations: `src/lib/api/mutations/use{Domain}.ts`.
- Defaults: 5min stale/gc, `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`.
- Mutations: `onSuccess` → `queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.<domain>.all })`.
- API client: `apiClient` from `src/lib/api/client.ts` — auto-attaches `Authorization`, `x-tenant-id`, `Accept-Language`, `Idempotency-Key` on POST.

### Forms
- TanStack Form + Zod — NOT react-hook-form.
- Use `useAppForm` / `withForm` from `src/shared/form/useAppForm.ts`.
- Pattern: `<form.AppForm><form.TextField name="..." /></form.AppForm>`.
- Zod schemas in `features/*/schemas/` or inline.

### UI (MUI v7)
- Page shell: `PageContainer` + `PageHeader`.
- Dialogs: `*FormDialog.tsx`, `ResponsiveDialog`.
- RBAC: `IfAllowed`, `RequireAuth` from `src/lib/rbac/components.tsx`.
- Theme: `createAppTheme()` + `ThemeProvider` reads `usePreferencesStore` (light/dark, RTL/LTR).
- Notifications: `useNotification()` — not raw `useNotificationStore` in components.

### React Hooks ESLint (React 19)
- No `setState` in `useEffect` — derive during render, dialog `onEntered`/`handleClose`, or render-time key reset.
- No `ref.current` in JSX or during render — use `useState` for displayed values; update refs in effects.
- See `docs/skills/05-react-hooks-eslint.md` for approved patterns.

### Routing & i18n
- TanStack Router; URL pattern: `/:lang/app/<feature>`.
- Auth-gated router swap: `upgradeRouterWithAppRoutes()` / `downgradeRouterForPublicAccess()`.
- Navigation: `{domain}ModuleNav` registered in `app/navigation/moduleRegistry.ts`.
- i18n: `useTranslation()` + `useI18nFormat()` for numbers/dates/currency.
- `LocaleSwitcher` + `langRoute.beforeLoad` sync URL ↔ locale ↔ direction.
- Typed keys via `src/lib/i18n/i18next.d.ts`; languages: `en`, `ar` (RTL).

### Naming
- Pages: `{Name}Page.tsx`; hooks: `use{Entity}`, `use{Action}{Entity}`.
- Permissions mirror backend: `action:resource` in `lib/rbac/backend-permissions.ts`.

## Cross-Cutting
- Refer to `docs/skills/` for domain flows and module dependency map.
- POS sync creates `SalesOrder` only — no auto-invoice/stock-issue.
- `InventoryPostingService` is the GL bridge for stock movements.
- `ApprovalService` (Sales-owned) gates Invoice and VendorBill posting.
